0..79 Comment "// Univalence over the user universe, after the HoTT book\'s § 2.10 and cubical"
80..146 Comment "// Agda\'s `Cubical/Foundations/Univalence.agda`. `ua(e)` makes the"
147..216 Comment "// bi-invertible map `e : A ≃ B` between two types of `Type` a path"
217..302 Comment "// `Path[.A = Type](A, B)`, admitted on the record\'s two laws as its evidence, at any"
303..377 Comment "// two codes: two variables, or a path type and a presented type, which no"
378..455 Comment "// finite round-trip coverage reaches. Transport along it applies the map, by"
456..533 Comment "// conversion (cubical\'s `uaβ`) and by a run. Transport along a path between"
534..605 Comment "// types, packaged as the record, is `idtoequiv` (the book\'s `idtoeqv`,"
606..683 Comment "// cubical\'s `pathToEquiv`); `ua` and `idtoequiv` make a quasi-inverse and so"
684..758 Comment "// an equivalence, `univalence`, on two owed laws: `ua` after `idtoequiv`,"
759..838 Comment "// which no rule converts, and `idtoequiv` after `ua`, which needs the record\'s"
839..879 Comment "// inverses to be determined by its map."
880..882 Comment "//"
883..924 Comment "// - see: #650 — `oneBack`, `idtoequiv`"
925..955 Comment "// - see: #695 — `idtoequiv`"
956..986 Comment "// - see: #698 — `idtoequiv`"
987..1029 Comment "// - see: #1979 — `loopsAreTheirWinding`"
1030..1056 Comment "// - see: #520 — `uaEta`"
1057..1088 Comment "// - see: #656 — `univalence`"
